f46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_ubuntu_timeseries.csv) (with vertical dashed lines marking the 6 barriers).\n   - **What it proves:** Visually shows the 6 phases in action—RAM stepping up after Deploy (50 containers), doubling during Verify Setup (100 containers), and returning cleanly to baseline after Teardown with zero memory leaks.\n\n5. **Per-Step CPU & I/O Wait Utilization (Grouped Bar Chart)**\n   - **Data:** `cpu_avg_pct`, `cpu_max_pct`, and `iowait_avg_pct` per `step_name` from [`thesis_ubuntu_step_resources.csv`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_ubuntu_step_resources.csv).\n   - **What it proves:** That the host CPU remains well below saturation (~20–23% average across 8 cores) even during 100-container bursts."}
