{"step_index":659,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T20:03:12Z","input_tokens":2726,"cache_read_tokens":234580,"output_tokens":847,"content":"I have generated both **Graph 1** and **Graph 2** in publication-ready 300 DPI PNG and vector PDF format (for direct inclusion in LaTeX using `\\includegraphics{...}`).\n\n---\n\n### Graph 1: Cold Deploy Create vs. ZFS CoW Clone Latency\n- **Files:**\n  - PNG: [graph1_cow_vs_deploy.png](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph1_cow_vs_deploy.png)\n  - PDF: [graph1_cow_vs_deploy.pdf](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph1_cow_vs_deploy.pdf)\n  - Remote: `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_figures/graph1_cow_vs_deploy.pdf`\n- **Key Takeaway for Thesis:**\n  - Shows side-by-side comparison between **Alpine Linux (3.21 MiB)** and **Ubuntu Heavy (~1.5 GB)** across all 9 scaling tiers (from 2 up to 100 peak concurrent containers).\n  - Demonstrates that as concurrency scales to 100 peak containers ($M=10, N=5$), cold image unpacking (`Deploy Create`) jumps to **76.2s** on Ubuntu, whereas ZFS snapshot cloning (`CoW Clone`) takes only **22.2s** (**$3.4\\times$ speedup** on Ubuntu, **$3.6\\times$ speedup** on Alpine).\n\n---\n\n### Graph 2: Micro-Phase Latency Breakdown at Scale (Stacked Bar Chart)\n- **Files:**\n  - PNG: [graph2_microphase_breakdown.png](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph2_microphase_breakdown.png)\n  - PDF: [graph2_microphase_breakdown.pdf](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/thesis_figures/graph2_microphase_breakdown.pdf)\n  - Remote: `/home/debian/bluectfd/thesis_figures/graph2_microphase_breakdown.pdf`\n- **Key Takeaway for Thesis:**\n  - **Panel A (Deploy):** Clearly illustrates that instance creation (image rootfs unpacking) is the single overwhelming bottleneck during cold provisioning (~80% of total time).\n  - **Panel B (Verify Setup):** Shows how the ephemeral sandbox lifecycle is distributed across OVN logical switch creation, ZFS CoW cloning, NIC rebinding, and container boot. Shows that OVN switch creation scales with team count $M$, while cloning scales with container count $M \\times N$.\n\nThe generation script is saved at [`plot_thesis_graphs.py`](file:///home/davidel/.gemini/antigravity/brain/335ea41a-df46-4ffa-bb4c-eefc5a5248cd/scratch/plot_thesis_graphs.py) should you wish to tweak colors, fonts, or styling."}
